# Image TODO: hami-fakegpu-on-k3s-v1.png

## Purpose
Show the two operators on the k3s playground and what each one does:
fake-gpu-operator invents the GPUs, HAMi schedules against them.

## Composition breakdown
- Left: a namespace card "gpu-operator" containing four small pod boxes labeled
  "device-plugin", "status-updater", "topology-server", "nvidia-dcgm-exporter",
  with caption "fabricates nvidia.com/gpu — no hardware".
- Right: a namespace card "kube-system" containing one pod box "hami-scheduler
  (2/2)" split into two containers "scheduler" and "webhook", caption "decides GPU
  placement".
- Center/bottom: a worker node card with a green GPU chip and node labels
  "nvidia.com/gpu.product=Tesla-K80" and "run.ai/simulated-gpu-node-pool=default".
- Arrows: fake-gpu-operator → node (writing capacity); HAMi → node (reading it).

## Gemini prompt
